 "title": "is one tail closer to mattering than the other, on one ruler?",
 "verdict": "the_wide_tail_is_the_only_tail_that_can_reach_a_row",
 "verdict_reason": "2 row(s) sit at a published multiplier past their flip: wide [9, 13] / tight []; every published p05 is >= 1.0000 while 10 of 12 flips need a multiplier LARGER than 1 (so a smaller multiplier cannot re-enter them); 10 of 12 scored row(s) put the wide tail closer on the normalised ruler, 2 the tight tail, 0 tie -- the tight end is inert here, but inert because the population never publishes a narrowing multiplier, not because the tight tail is safe"
